            <ArticleTitle>Weight Management and Exercise for Cancer Survivors.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>129-32</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1188/16.CJON.129-132</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Obesity may contribute to development and recurrence of cancer, as well as cancer-related and all-cause mortality. This risk factor is also among the most preventable causes of cancer. This article describes current evidence-based guidelines for weight management and physical activity for cancer survivors. The authors also discuss practical interventions to help survivors undertake behavioral changes to manage their weight.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
